@startuml lsl-pi-format-pipeline
!include _standard-style.puml

title LSL pi Session Format - Write Path, Backfill and Viewer

top to bottom direction

package "Sources" {
  [Agent transcript\n(Claude / Copilot / OpenCode)] as Src <<external>>
  database "Legacy markdown\n3 dialects, 22.5k files" as MD <<storage>>
}

package "Conversion" {
  [ConfigurableRedactor] as Redactor <<util>>
  [LslMarkdownParser] as Parser <<core>>
  [backfill-lsl-to-pi.mjs] as Backfill <<cli>>
  [PiSessionWriter] as Writer <<core>>
}

package "Corpus" {
  database "pi session JSONL\nYYYY/MM tranches" as JL <<storage>>
  database "quarantine/\n+ chain-map.json" as QT <<storage>>
}

package "Read path" {
  [lsl-sessions.mjs] as Api <<api>>
  [pi export shell\n+ light palette] as Shell <<util>>
  [Sessions tab] as Tab <<api>>
}

Src --> Redactor : every exchange
Redactor --> Writer : sanitized
MD --> Backfill : one CHAIN at a time
Backfill --> Parser
Parser --> Writer : shared entry emitter
Writer DATA_LINE JL
Backfill OPTIONAL_LINE QT : unconvertible —\nmarkdown kept
JL --> Api
Api --> Shell
Shell --> Tab

note right of Redactor
  Runs on EVERY exchange, on the main
  thread — a backtracking pattern here
  wedges the ETM while it stays alive.
end note

note right of Backfill
  The unit of work is a CHAIN, not a file:
  rotation splits MID-TOKEN, so a part
  cannot be parsed on its own. Every chain
  is verified BEFORE its markdown is removed.
end note

note right of Writer
  One emitter for both paths, so live and
  backfilled output cannot diverge.
end note

@enduml
